{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.HeckeAlgebra","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.ArchimedeanRealization","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PermutationEnumeration"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.extended_upstream_discharge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.extended_upstream_discharge","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L410-L428","doc":"**Master+ aggregate**: extends `complete_upstream_discharge`\nwith Wedderburn iso n=4..8 + H_4 block dims.\n\n**Narrowed 2026-08-21**: the Lie-valued-Stokes conjunct (and with it\nthe now-unused `M`, `𝔤` parameters) was removed together with\n`lie_valued_stokes_discharged` — see the removal note above; that\nobligation is not discharged, so the aggregate must not claim it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.H4_block_dims_discharged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.H4_block_dims_discharged","kind":"theorem","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L353-L356","doc":"**H_4 block dimensions discharged** via the cohort tables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.wedderburn_n4_to_n8_discharged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.wedderburn_n4_to_n8_discharged","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L339-L351","doc":"**Wedderburn iso n=4..8 discharged**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.complete_upstream_discharge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.complete_upstream_discharge","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L301-L330","doc":"**Final aggregate**: at any commutative ring `R` with\nparameter `q : R`, marker element `z : ℝ`, the upstream\n`QOU.Mathlib.*` infrastructure discharges:\n- GB spectral-sequence collapse at E_2,\n- Wedderburn iso at n = 2, 3,\n- Markov-axiom recursion at H_1 → H_2 and H_2 → H_3,\n- Substrate q₀ regime,\n- Existence of Yekutieli finite-slice trace.\nAll as concrete (non-vacuous) theorems. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.simple_transposition_self_inverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.simple_transposition_self_inverse","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L287-L294","doc":"**Bridge theorem**: every simple transposition σ_i is its\nown inverse (= identity property of the simple\nCoxeter generators). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.markov_axiom_recursion_discharged_low_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.markov_axiom_recursion_discharged_low_n","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L268-L279","doc":"**Aggregate**: the Markov-axiom recursion is discharged\nat every level n ∈ {1, 2}; level n ≥ 3 is tractable via\n`canonical_lift` with caller-supplied per-level data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.markov_axiom_h2_to_h3_discharged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.markov_axiom_h2_to_h3_discharged","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L258-L266","doc":"**Bridge theorem**: the Markov-axiom recursion is discharged at\nH_2 → H_3 — instance plus holding Markov axiom.  Restated\n2026-08-21 for the same reason as the H_1 → H_2 case above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.markov_axiom_h1_to_h2_discharged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.markov_axiom_h1_to_h2_discharged","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L241-L256","doc":"**Bridge theorem**: the Markov-axiom recursion is discharged at\nH_1 → H_2 — the upstream concrete instance exists *and its Markov\naxiom actually holds*.\n\n**Restated 2026-08-21** (vacuity ledger, `exists-true-tautology`).\nWas `∃ M : MarkovTraceRecursionWithMul ℝ 1 q z, True`.  The witness\nwas always real (`h1_to_h2`, a genuine construction), but the\n`∃ _, True` conclusion threw away everything it satisfies — which\nis the part `_discharged` was claiming.  The `axiom_witness` field\nis now exposed in the statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.upstream_discharge_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.upstream_discharge_complete","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L217-L231","doc":"**Master discharge theorem**: for every QOU-relevant Hecke\nlevel `n ∈ {2..6}` and any commutative ring `R` + parameter\n`q : R`, the upstream infrastructure provides:\n- a Wedderburn isomorphism instance,\n- the Σ d_λ² = n! cardinality witness via cohort,\n- the GB spectral-sequence collapse-at-E_2 instance,\nall without recourse to upstream-Mathlib substrate axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.yekutieli_finite_slice_discharged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.yekutieli_finite_slice_discharged","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L185-L209","doc":"**Substrate-discharger**: the finite-slice axioms *determine* the\nYekutieli multiplicative trace — for any group `G` with marked\nelement `z : G`, every trace satisfying them is `z ^ n`.\n\n**Restated 2026-08-21** (vacuity ledger, `exists-true-tautology`).\nWas `∃ Y : YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace G z, True :=\n⟨inferInstance, trivial⟩` — i.e. \"the instance that already\nresolves, resolves\".  `∃ _, True` discards everything the witness\nsatisfies, which is precisely what the name `_discharged` claims;\nexhibiting an instance is not discharging an obligation.  Now\ndelegates to `yekutieli_finite_slice_substrate`, so the name is\nbacked by a falsifiable statement.\n\n**Converges with `246334be7c`** (sibling session, landed on `main`),\nwhich drained the same four defects in this file by rewriting\n`∃ X, True` as `Nonempty X`.  That is right as far as it goes — for a\n*content-bearing* carrier like `YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace`\n(`trace_zero` + `trace_succ`), `Nonempty` is a genuine claim.  This\nextends it: `Nonempty` still only says an instance resolves, which the\ninstance declaration already established, whereas the statement below\nsays the axioms **determine** the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.wedderburn_iso_n2_to_n6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.wedderburn_iso_n2_to_n6","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L164-L176","doc":"**Substrate-discharger**: at every QOU-relevant Hecke\nlevel `n ∈ {2..6}`, the Wedderburn-block dimensions sum to\n`n.factorial`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.substrate_q0_in_regime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.substrate_q0_in_regime","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L152-L154","doc":"**Substrate `q_0 > 1` discharge**: the QOU substrate\nparameter is in the analytic-continuation regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.archimedean_eval_well_defined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.archimedean_eval_well_defined","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L130-L150","doc":"**Scalar Archimedean discharge**: the real-valued evaluation at the\nsubstrate point is *unique*.  Any ring homomorphism `ℝ[q] → ℝ` that\nfixes the constants and sends `q ↦ q₀` **is** `evalAtQZero` — so the\nsubstrate axiom's `Real_q₀` is determined by its defining properties\nrather than merely asserted to exist.  This is the chain-independent\npiece of the Archimedean realisation.\n\nThe previous statement was `∃ y : ℝ, evalAtQZero p = y`, which holds\nfor every total function into an inhabited type and so discharged\nnothing: \"well-defined\" is not a theorem in a total type theory.\nExistence of the evaluation is `evalAtQZero` itself; what a discharge\nowes is that it is a ring map (`evalAtQZero_add` / `_mul` / `_C` /\n`_X` in `ArchimedeanRealization`) and that nothing else is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.rsk_cardinality_discharged_n2_to_n8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.rsk_cardinality_discharged_n2_to_n8","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L91-L112","doc":"**Substrate-discharger**: for every `n ∈ {2..8}`, there\nexists a `CohortRSKWitness n` (no upstream Mathlib RSK\nneeded). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.exists_collapsing_spectralSequence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpstreamSubstrateBridge.exists_collapsing_spectralSequence","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean#L71-L81","doc":"**The API is inhabited**: some spectral sequence over `R` collapses at\n`E_2`, witnessed by the trivial model.\n\nWas `gb_spectral_collapse_at_E2_discharged`, which read as though the\nsubstrate axiom had been discharged. Nothing here mentions the Gröbner\nfiltration, and the witness performs no computation: the statement is\n`∃ S, CollapsesAtE2 S`, which the constant-zero differential satisfies\ndefinitionally. Renamed so the name matches the content. ","signatureChunk":0}]}